    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Object Creation & Setter Approach Deep Dive -->
    <div class="card page-break">
        <h2>4. Deep Dive: Object Creation & Setters Approach</h2>
        <p>Aapne pucha tha ki <strong>"Service me Object kaha ban raha hai aur value kaha set ho rahi hai?"</strong></p>
        
        <p>Code me standard, traditional <strong>new keyword + Setter methods</strong> use hue hain taaki code crystal-clear rahe:</p>

        <pre><code>// 1. Database se Foreign Key Entities fetch ki
Company company = companyRepository.findById(request.getCompanyId()).orElseThrow(...);
Department department = departmentRepository.findById(request.getDepartmentId()).orElseThrow(...);

// 2. new keyword se Object BAN RAHA HAI aur SETTERS se VALUES SET HO RAHI HAIN:
Employee employee = new Employee();               // <-- YAHA JAVA MEMORY ME OBJECT CREATE HUA!
employee.setEmployeeCode(employeeCode);           // <-- VALUE SET HO RAHI HAI
employee.setFirstName(request.getFirstName());    // <-- VALUE SET HO RAHI HAI
employee.setLastName(request.getLastName());      // <-- VALUE SET HO RAHI HAI
employee.setEmail(request.getEmail());            // <-- VALUE SET HO RAHI HAI
employee.setJoiningDate(request.getJoiningDate());// <-- VALUE SET HO RAHI HAI
employee.setCompany(company);                     // <-- Company Entity SET hui
employee.setDepartment(department);               // <-- Department Entity SET hui
employee.setDesignation(designation);             // <-- Designation Entity SET hui
employee.setManager(manager);                     // <-- Reporting Manager SET hua

// 3. Database me Permanent Save:
Employee savedEmployee = employeeRepository.save(employee); // <-- SQL INSERT execute hua

// 4. Response DTO Object Creation & Setting (mapToResponse):
EmployeeResponse response = new EmployeeResponse(); // <-- DTO OBJECT CREATE HUA!
response.setId(savedEmployee.getId());              // <-- ID SET
response.setEmployeeCode(savedEmployee.getEmployeeCode()); // <-- Code SET
response.setFullName(savedEmployee.getFullName());  // <-- Name SET
response.setDepartmentName(savedEmployee.getDepartment().getName()); // <-- Dept Name SET
return response;                                    // <-- Controller ko return</code></pre>

        <div class="alert alert-success">
            <strong>Fayda:</strong> Is tarike se bilkul clearly dikhta hai ki kab <code>new Employee()</code> ya <code>new EmployeeResponse()</code> se blank object bana, aur kab ek-ek line me <code>.setXYZ(...)</code> se values assign hui!
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5: Under the Hood Request Flow -->
    <div class="card">
        <h2>5. Request Lifecycle: Postman se Database Tak</h2>
        <p>Jab aap Postman se <code>POST /api/v1/employees</code> request bhejte hain, to step-by-step kya hota hai:</p>

        <ol>
            <li><strong>Client:</strong> Postman Header me JWT token bhejta hai: <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code></li>
            <li><strong>JwtAuthenticationFilter:</strong> Filter token ko intercept karta hai, JJWT library se secret key verify karta hai, aur authenticated user ko Spring Security Context me store karta hai.</li>
            <li><strong>Authorization Check:</strong> <code>@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('SUPER_ADMIN', 'HR_ADMIN')")</code> check karta hai ki kya user ke paas Admin authority hai. Agar nahi, to <code>403 Forbidden</code> return ho jata hai.</li>
            <li><strong>Controller Validation:</strong> <code>@Valid @RequestBody CreateEmployeeRequest request</code> se check hota hai ki first name, email, joining date empty to nahi hai.</li>
            <li><strong>Service Business Logic:</strong> <code>EmployeeService</code> email duplication check karta hai, unique Employee Code generate karta hai, aur entity save karta hai.</li>
            <li><strong>Database Save:</strong> Spring Data JPA PostgreSQL me <code>INSERT INTO employees</code> aur <code>INSERT INTO users</code> run karta hai.</li>
            <li><strong>JSON Output:</strong> Service response DTO banata hai, aur Jackson usko JSON me convert karke HTTP 201 Created return karta hai.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

